id: quiz.rust.bounded-concurrency
kind: quiz
track: rust
title: Bounding concurrency
question: You need to process 10k items against an upstream API. How do you do it without falling over?
expects:
  - semaphore
  - bounded
  - backpressure
  - timeout
  - retry jitter
misuse:
  - unbounded spawn => memory grows with input and the upstream is hammered
  - join all => unbounded fan-out in disguise
related:
  - rust.bounded-concurrency
  - rust.tokio-semaphore
  - rust.retry
  - design.backpressure
follow_ups:
  - what happens when the upstream starts returning 429?
answer: |
  Stream with buffered/buffer_unordered or a Semaphore permit per item, so at
  most N are in flight; timeouts per attempt, jittered retries on idempotent
  calls, and a total budget. On 429, slow down (respect Retry-After) and shed
  rather than queue.
